[[:db/retract 17592186125189 :question/answer-fields 17592186123734] {:db/id 17592186124462 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6f16c0b1-b80b-5067-adaf-a65b04fb7bb4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6f16c0b1-b80b-5067-adaf-a65b04fb7bb4" :question/id #uuid "6f16c0b1-b80b-5067-adaf-a65b04fb7bb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-130721" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve ${e}^{{x}^{2}y}={y}^{2}-{x}^{3}+9.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}y} & ={y}^{2}-{x}^{3}+9 \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}y}-{y}^{2}+{x}^{3} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={e}^{{x}^{2}y}-{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=9.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(2,0)$ can be found by computing $∇f(2,0).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(2,0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y}-{y}^{2}+{x}^{3})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{{x}^{2}y}-{y}^{2}+{x}^{3})j \\\\  & =(2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}+3{x}^{2})i+({x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-2y)j \\\\ ∇f(2,0) & =(2(2)(0){e}^{({2}^{2})(0)}+3({2}^{2}))i+(({2}^{2}){e}^{({2}^{2})(0)}-2(0))j \\\\  & =12\\,i+4\\,j \\\\  & =⟨12,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(2,0)=⟨12,4⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(2,0).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-2}{12} & =\\frac{y-0}{4} \\\\ 4(x-2) & =12y \\\\ x-2 & =3y \\\\ x-3y-2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-02401848-522e-501b-82ff-6e5cb3f48ab9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02401848-522e-501b-82ff-6e5cb3f48ab9" :answer-field/id #uuid "02401848-522e-501b-82ff-6e5cb3f48ab9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-82ce7cc2-be21-5dc4-9b04-e941ddd03d24" :answer-field/choices ["answer-364ddf2b-cdd1-5e21-88c2-478a7d637e32" "answer-415a3975-289f-5c0a-aa48-bc85b813f82a" "answer-6321cb0e-8e68-5a7b-9a36-ac871cc17b89" "answer-ba63a292-9d83-540d-ac68-00ce4812ebb4" "answer-82ce7cc2-be21-5dc4-9b04-e941ddd03d24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-364ddf2b-cdd1-5e21-88c2-478a7d637e32" :answer/id #uuid "364ddf2b-cdd1-5e21-88c2-478a7d637e32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+3y-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-415a3975-289f-5c0a-aa48-bc85b813f82a" :answer/id #uuid "415a3975-289f-5c0a-aa48-bc85b813f82a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-y-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6321cb0e-8e68-5a7b-9a36-ac871cc17b89" :answer/id #uuid "6321cb0e-8e68-5a7b-9a36-ac871cc17b89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2y-2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba63a292-9d83-540d-ac68-00ce4812ebb4" :answer/id #uuid "ba63a292-9d83-540d-ac68-00ce4812ebb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3y-2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82ce7cc2-be21-5dc4-9b04-e941ddd03d24" :answer/id #uuid "82ce7cc2-be21-5dc4-9b04-e941ddd03d24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3y-2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-4c8248e9-9c46-5103-ac9c-f0a394655226" :activity/id #uuid "4c8248e9-9c46-5103-ac9c-f0a394655226" :activity/title "The Gradient as a Normal Vector" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050027 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-6fe264a7-c045-5612-8184-b7672b802421" "step-80a30235-ea9e-5be6-ade1-4b81b30de9fc" "step-20ee70ca-88be-504d-b7aa-237d8d22e58a" "step-68e1c4ea-40a6-5a21-ae75-071da89109f6" "step-1470ea07-3b96-5965-8beb-c2e0041edd4a"] :activit